From 76be70e4f54932a637fe17b07c0ab797a5751458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:41:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pages): null hidden object-list item TextTemplates under
 nested visibility rules (closes #1198)

A pluggable widget whose editorConfig hides an object-list ITEM
sub-property (a nested rule, ListPropertyKey set) kept the shipped
default text in that item's required TextTemplate even while the rule
hid it. Studio Pro stores null there, so mx check reported CE0463.

Found on File Uploader 2.5.0: allowedFileFormats[].typeFormatDescription
is a required TextTemplate hidden when configMode = "simple", so every
simple-mode format failed mx check.

ApplyVisibilityRules now skips nested rules at the top level and
evaluates them per item: when the rule is determinable from the item's
own primitive values and fires, that item's TextTemplate is nulled.
Only the hidden direction and only TextTemplate values are touched; an
indeterminable rule leaves the item unchanged.

Tested: make test (84 packages ok), gofmt, go vet.
Mendix 11.12.2: simple-mode .txt format plus advanced .zip format,
mx check 0 errors, runtime upload of both files stored, downloaded
bytes sha256-equal to source (2/2), .csv rejected by the widget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DyrzWc5YejD1iBLgJ7TS7q
